### Pruebas con la extensión REST Client de VS Code
@gateway = http://localhost:8080
# Pegue aquí un ID token de Firebase (ver README, sección "Obtener un token")
@token = PEGAR_TOKEN

### 1. Salud del gateway (pública) -> 200
GET {{gateway}}/health

### 2. Ruta protegida SIN token -> 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/products

### 3. Token falso -> 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer token-falso

### 4. Listar productos (MongoDB) -> 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Crear producto (MongoDB) -> 201
POST {{gateway}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Audífonos", "category": "Tecnología", "price": 80000, "stock": 5 }

### 6. Crear pedido (valida producto y stock en MongoDB, guarda en Oracle) -> 201
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "product_id": "PEGAR_ID_PRODUCTO", "quantity": 2, "customer_name": "Cliente Demo" }

### 7. Pedido con producto inexistente -> 400
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "product_id": "000000000000000000000000", "quantity": 1, "customer_name": "Cliente Demo" }

### 8. Listar pedidos (Oracle) -> 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Cambiar estado del pedido -> 200
PATCH {{gateway}}/api/orders/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "enviado" }

### 10. Estado de los microservicios (prueba de fallas) -> 200
GET {{gateway}}/health/services

### 11. Crear cliente (MongoDB, base tienda_clientes) -> 201
POST {{gateway}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cliente Demo", "email": "demo@correo.com", "phone": "3000000000", "city": "Bogotá" }

### 12. Listar clientes -> 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
